message.content:
I found two periapical lesions, both over the root-canal-treated upper front teeth. I graded them from enhanced crops of `radiograph.jpg`.

1. **Upper left central/lateral incisors (FDI teeth 21/22, right side of the image), PAI 4.** There is a clearly bounded dark (radiolucent) area just above and beside the tip of the root-filled tooth.
2. **Upper right central incisor (FDI tooth 11, left of the midline in the image), PAI 3.** There is a less clearly bounded area of thinner, mineral-depleted bone near the root tip. It sits close to the midline, so it could partly be the normal incisive canal. That makes this one less certain.

I did not count two other areas as lesions. The lower right first molar has a dark area between its roots, but that looks like furcation (root-split) bone loss rather than a lesion at the root tip. The badly decayed upper left molars showed no clear dark area at their root tips.

